From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:51:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: do not require FLAC++ to find FLAC

FindFLAC fails unless both libFLAC and libFLAC++ are found. FluidSynth
does not use FLAC itself. The module is only reached through
libsndfile's SndFileConfig.cmake, whose find_dependency(FLAC) picks up
this module ahead of libsndfile's own because cmake_admin is already on
CMAKE_MODULE_PATH. libsndfile links only FLAC::FLAC.

With a libFLAC built without the C++ library, the SndFile config is
rejected, FluidSynth falls back to FindSndFileLegacy, and SF3 support
is disabled even though libsndfile has Ogg/Vorbis support.

Require only the C library, and create FLAC::FLAC++ only when the C++
library is found.
---
 cmake_admin/FindFLAC.cmake | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cmake_admin/FindFLAC.cmake b/cmake_admin/FindFLAC.cmake
index 2de2f41a81da..0279daa49524 100644
--- a/cmake_admin/FindFLAC.cmake
+++ b/cmake_admin/FindFLAC.cmake
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ Result Variables
 This will define the following variables:
 
 ``FLAC_FOUND``
-  True if both libraries were found.
+  True if the C library was found.
 ``FLAC_FLAC_FOUND``
   True if the C library was found.
 ``FLAC_FLAC++_FOUND``
@@ -74,8 +74,7 @@ endif()
 # Forward the result to CMake
 include(FindPackageHandleStandardArgs)
 find_package_handle_standard_args(
-  FLAC REQUIRED_VARS "FLAC_LIBRARY" "FLAC_INCLUDE_DIR" "FLAC++_LIBRARY"
-                     "FLAC++_INCLUDE_DIR")
+  FLAC REQUIRED_VARS "FLAC_LIBRARY" "FLAC_INCLUDE_DIR")
 
 # Create the target
 if(FLAC_FOUND AND NOT TARGET FLAC::FLAC)
@@ -90,7 +89,10 @@ if(FLAC_FOUND AND NOT TARGET FLAC::FLAC)
   set(FLAC_FLAC_FOUND TRUE)
 endif()
 
-if(FLAC_FOUND AND NOT TARGET FLAC::FLAC++)
+if(FLAC_FOUND
+   AND FLAC++_LIBRARY
+   AND FLAC++_INCLUDE_DIR
+   AND NOT TARGET FLAC::FLAC++)
   add_library(FLAC::FLAC++ UNKNOWN IMPORTED)
   set_target_properties(
     FLAC::FLAC++
